  "details": "I'm having issues with my quest 3 controllers where my gestures are not properly detected. Until yesterday, I thought that it was just a hardware issue. But I found out that when avatar gestures are disabled in the action menu, gesture detection actually worked almost perfectly (but with different animations). Weird, right?\n\nThis feels like both hardware and software issue combined as not everyone has it.\n\nExtra info:\n\n- My left controller was affected the most. Usually got stuck in the peace gesture.\n\n- My avatar has no FX layer related to hand gestures.\n\n- VRChat build 1727 (but the issue existed for more than a year)\n\n- Kubuntu 25.04 (not relevant as it was happening on Windows 11 too)\n\n- KDE Plasma 6.3.4 (on Wayland)\n\n- Kernel version: 6.14.0-34-generic (64-bit)\n\n- ALVR v20.14.1 (this is what I use to connect my Quest 3 to my PC over WiFi)",
